<Base title="Privacy Policy | SilTest Semiconductors" description="How SilTest Semiconductors GmbH collects, uses, stores, and protects personal data, and your rights under GDPR.">
  <Header />
  <section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv in"><span class="eyebrow">Legal</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1></div></div></section>
  <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap legal rv">

    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <p>The controller responsible for data processing on this website is:</p>
    <p>SilTest Semiconductors GmbH<br />
    Lindenstra&szlig;e 64, 47533 Kleve, Germany<br />
    Managing Director: Sameer Saran<br />
    Telephone: +49 (0)2821 / 5904460<br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:info@siltest.com">info@siltest.com</a></p>
    <p>The controller is the person who decides on the purposes and means of processing personal data.</p>

    <h2>2. Data protection officer</h2>
    <p>We are not legally required to appoint a data protection officer. For any question about your data, please contact us at <a href="mailto:info@siltest.com">info@siltest.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>3. Hosting and content delivery</h2>
    <p>This website is a static site hosted by GitHub, Inc. (GitHub Pages), 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. It is delivered through the content delivery network of Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA.</p>
    <p>When you visit the site, these providers process technical connection data such as your IP address, the requested page, browser type, and the time of the request. This is necessary to deliver the site securely and reliably and to defend against attacks. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in a secure and efficient online offering (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR).</p>
    <p>These providers are based in the USA. Where personal data is transferred to the USA, the transfer is based on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework where the provider is certified under it, and otherwise on the Standard Contractual Clauses of the European Commission.</p>
    <!-- VERIFY before launch: confirm the current transfer safeguard for GitHub and Cloudflare (Data Privacy Framework certification or SCCs) and, if you want, add a data processing agreement reference. -->

    <h2>4. Fonts</h2>
    <p>This website uses the IBM Plex font family for a consistent appearance. The fonts are installed locally and are served from our own site. No connection to Google servers is made and no font data is sent to third parties.</p>

    <h2>5. Cookies and tracking</h2>
    <p>This website does not use analytics, advertising, or tracking cookies. It does not use Google Analytics, the LinkedIn Insight Tag, or similar tracking tools.</p>
    <p>Our content delivery provider may set technically necessary cookies that are required to deliver the site securely. These are used on the basis of our legitimate interest in secure delivery (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR) and are not used to track you across sites.</p>
    <p>Because we do not set non-essential cookies, this site does not show a cookie consent banner. If we add analytics or marketing tools in the future, we will ask for your consent before they load, in line with Section 25 (1) TDDDG.</p>

    <h2>6. Contact form and contact by email</h2>
    <p>When you send us a message through the contact form, we process the data you enter, such as your name, email address, company, and message, to handle your request and any follow-up questions. Our contact form is processed by our form provider, Formspree, Inc., 2100 Geng Road, Suite 210, Palo Alto, CA 94303, USA, which forwards submissions to us by email.</p>
    <p>If you contact us directly by email or telephone, we process the details you provide in order to answer your request.</p>
    <p>The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR where your request relates to a contract or pre-contractual steps, and otherwise our legitimate interest in answering enquiries (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR). Where a transfer to the USA takes place through our form provider, it is based on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework where the provider is certified under it, and otherwise on the Standard Contractual Clauses of the European Commission.</p>
    <p>We keep this data until your request is fully handled, unless statutory retention periods require longer storage.</p>
    <!-- VERIFY before launch: confirm the current transfer safeguard for Formspree. If you later move the form to a provider inside the EU, update this section. -->

    <h2>7. Payment services</h2>
    <p>When you buy an Academy course or a tool subscription, the payment is handled on the hosted checkout pages of Stripe. The European provider is Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd., 1 Grand Canal Street Lower, Grand Canal Dock, Dublin, Ireland. Stripe collects the data needed to process your payment, such as your name, contact details, and payment information, directly on its own pages. We do not receive or store full payment card details.</p>
    <p>The legal basis is the performance of a contract with you (Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR). Stripe's own privacy information applies to the data you enter during checkout.</p>

    <h2>8. Embedded videos (YouTube)</h2>
    <p>Some pages may embed videos from YouTube using the extended data protection mode (youtube-nocookie.com), operated by Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland. A video only loads after you actively click to play it. Until you click, no connection to YouTube is made.</p>
    <p>When you start a video, a connection to YouTube is established and YouTube receives which page you visited. In the extended data protection mode YouTube states that it does not set cookies for this purpose, but it may store comparable information in your browser. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in presenting our content (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR), and your consent through your click where required (Art. 6 (1) (a) GDPR and Section 25 (1) TDDDG). Google's own privacy policy applies to any further processing.</p>

    <h2>9. Customer relationship management</h2>
    <p>[PLACEHOLDER: Confirm whether enquiries received through this website are imported into a CRM such as HubSpot or Zoho. If yes, name the provider, its location, the purpose (managing contacts and follow-up), the legal basis (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR, our legitimate interest in managing business contacts), and the transfer safeguard for any processing outside the EU. If no CRM receives this data, this section can be removed.]</p>

    <h2>10. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Within the limits of the law, you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Access the personal data we hold about you (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Have inaccurate data corrected (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Have your data deleted (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Have processing restricted (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Receive your data in a portable format (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Object to processing based on legitimate interest (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent at any time, with effect for the future</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@siltest.com">info@siltest.com</a>.</p>
    <p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority. The authority responsible for our registered office is the State Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information North Rhine-Westphalia (Landesbeauftragte f&uuml;r Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit Nordrhein-Westfalen).</p>

    <h2>11. Objection to advertising emails</h2>
    <p>We object to the use of contact data published under our imprint obligation for sending advertising or information material that we did not request. We reserve the right to take legal steps if unsolicited advertising, for example spam email, is sent to us.</p>

    <h2>12. Encryption</h2>
    <p>This site uses SSL or TLS encryption to protect the content you send to us. You can recognise an encrypted connection by the "https://" prefix and the lock symbol in your browser bar.</p>

    <h2>13. Data retention</h2>
    <p>We keep personal data only as long as needed for the purpose for which it was collected, or as long as statutory retention periods require. After that, the data is deleted.</p>

    <h2>14. Updates to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy so that it always reflects the current processing on our website. The latest version is available at <a href="https://www.siltest.com/privacy/">www.siltest.com/privacy/</a>.</p>

  </div></section>
  <Footer />
</Base>
